      "body": "Here are some tests that show the problem in different places (i.e., a local fix to one of them might not fix the root issue):\r\n\r\n```python\r\n    @requires_curses_func('resize_term')\r\n    def test_resize_term_initscr_segfault(self):\r\n        curses.initscr()\r\n        lines = cols = 40000\r\n        try:\r\n            curses.resize_term(lines, cols)\r\n        except:\r\n            pass\r\n        curses.initscr()\r\n        curses.initscr()\r\n\r\n    @requires_curses_func('resizeterm')\r\n    def test_resizeterm_initscr_segfault(self):\r\n        curses.initscr()\r\n        lines = cols = 40000\r\n        try:\r\n            curses.resizeterm(lines, cols)\r\n        except:\r\n            pass\r\n        curses.initscr()\r\n        curses.initscr()\r\n\r\n    def test_resize_term_refresh_segfault(self):\r\n        curses.initscr()\r\n        lines = cols = 40000\r\n        try:\r\n            curses.resize_term(lines, cols)\r\n        except:\r\n            pass\r\n        c = curses.initscr()\r\n        c.refresh()\r\n```",
